00400              * COMMANDS:
00401              *         R               REGISTER TYPE
00402              *      (/)L               LOAD
00403              *         P (LOC,LOC)     PUNCH
00404              *         A LOC,VAL VAL...ALTER
00405              *        /A LOC,ASCII STRING
00406              *       //A REG           ALTER REG C, B, A, X, P OR
00407              *      (/)T LOC(,COUNT)   TYPE
00408              *         G LOC           GOTO
00410              *         Z LOC,LOC(,VAL) BLOCK INIT
00411              *         S LOC,VAL,MASK  SEARCH (MAX 2 BYTES)
00412              *         X (LOC,LOC)     CHECKSUM
00415              *         M FIRST,LAST,TO BLOCK MOVE
00420              *         W LOC           INSERT BLOCK
00430              *         I LOC,VAL VAL...INSERT
00440              *         Q               QUERRY ALL BREAKPOINTS
00450              *         B LOC(,LOC...)  SET BREAKPOINTS
00460              *         D (LOC,LOC...)  DELETE BREAKPOINTS
00470              *         N (LOC,LOC...)  NEXT BREAKPOINT
00480              *         H               HOLD BREAKPOINT AND GO
00490              *      (/)SPACE BAR       TYPE NEXT N LOCATIONS
00500              *         ; COUNT         DEFALT TYPE COUNT
00510              *         %               INITALIZE INTERCEPTS
00520              *
00552              *
00560              * NOTES:
00561              *         RXX IS REL ADDRESS REQUEST
00562              *         I WITHIN INSERT REFERS TO INSTR (AUTO SIZE
00563              *         J WITHIN INSERT REFERS TO JUMP BACK
00564              *         JN MEANS N BYTES AFTER INSERT POINT
00565              *         NO OVERFLOW CHECK ON BREAKPOINTS
00566              *         MAY NOT SET A BREAKPOINT IF ALREADY A 3F
00567              *            (BUT NO ERROR GIVEN)
00568              *         RESETTING NON-EXISTANT BREAKPOINT GIVES ? 
00569              *         ALL COMMANDS MUST END WITH 'CR'
00570              *         NEXT RESETS CURRENT BREAKPOINT, OPTIONALLY
00571              *            NEW ONES AND RESETS OLD BREAK LOCATOR
00572              *         RESET BREAKPOINTS WILL RESET ALL IF NONE D
00573              *         ASCII TYPE WILL ZERO PARITY BIT AND WILL T





